# linux/steward-desk-snapshot.service - one producer run: rebuild every
# principal's file into a fresh generation and swap the symlink onto it.
#
# Type=oneshot, because it is a ROUND and not a service - it writes a
# generation and exits, and the server in front of it never restarts. The two
# units are deliberately independent: a producer that cannot run leaves the
# desk serving the last good generation until it goes stale, which the server
# reports; a server that is down does not stop the generations from being
# written.
#
# KillMode=process for the reason agent-session@.service documents at length:
# without it systemd tidies the whole cgroup when the round exits. Nothing here
# is handed off today, but the round shells out (jq, git, the estate's liveness
# command) and a round that must not take its own children with it is the
# cheaper default.
#
# NO ENVIRONMENT LINES. The directory comes from desk/bin/desk-paths, the same
# bridge the server reads. See steward-desk.service.
[Unit]
Description=steward desk snapshot - rebuild the per-principal files

[Service]
Type=oneshot
KillMode=process
ExecStart=/bin/bash %h/scripts/desk/snapshot.sh
